"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative launched by Alex, with Sarah Tan as the lead and an initial budget of $500,000 for Phase One. The project kick-off was scheduled for June 15th. The team expanded in September with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. A significant milestone was reached in October with the successful completion of the testing phase for a secure file sharing prototype, ahead of schedule. Phase Two has achieved a breakthrough in predictive analytics, with a detailed report to be shared on November 20th. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. Additionally, the compliance plan's budget was increased to $55,000, and security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, will be updated effective January next year."
